.TH AVR\-RUN\-VIEW 1 "" "avr 0.1.3" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-run-view \- View a workflow run with its jobs.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr run view
[OPTIONS] [RUN_ID]
.SH DESCRIPTION
View a workflow run with its jobs.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Without RUN_ID, shows 10 most recent runs.
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr run view
    avr run view run-abc123
    avr run view run-abc123 --steps
    avr run view run-abc123 --log-failed
    avr run view run-abc123 --job Build
    avr run view run-abc123 --json conclusion,jobs
    avr run view run-abc123 --json '*' --jq '.jobs[].job_name'
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    conclusion, created_at, display_title, duration_seconds, event,
    head_branch, head_sha, jobs, platform_run_id, repository, run_attempt,
    run_id, run_number, status, triggering_actor, updated_at, workflow,
    workflow_id
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
[\fIRUN_ID\fR]
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-steps\fR
Expand each job to show its individual steps.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\fR
Print full logs for all jobs.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-failed\fR
Print logs only for failed steps.
.TP
\fB\-\-job\fR \fITEXT\fR
Restrict view and logs to jobs whose name contains this string.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.TP
\fB\-\-web\fR
Open in browser.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print logs directly to stdout instead of paging through `less`. Same as setting AVR_PAGER=''.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-run (1),
.BR avr-run-cancel (1),
.BR avr-run-list (1),
.BR avr-run-logs (1),
.BR avr-run-rerun (1),
.BR avr-run-watch (1)
